comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-13T21:59:23.505Z",codex-root,"Duplicate check 2026-07-13: prior all-status audits are completed point-in-time reviews and pm-e9zh owns terminal resolution evidence; none owns a future resumable typed-relationship reconstruction program. This plan starts only after pm-6x7o."
  "2026-07-31T10:17:21.616Z","harness:codex","Live reconstruction input 2026-07-31: complete all-status/current-state and immutable-activity snapshots were reviewed before mutation; no active isolate, missing active endpoint, parent-scope duplicate, or active ordering cycle exists. Wave 1 received only evidence-backed active prerequisites and semantic implementation/verification/provenance edges. The remaining 11 graph findings are terminal-only information and stay in the dedicated changelog-safe waves; no closed item was rewritten opportunistically."
  "2026-08-01T20:21:49.469Z","harness:codex","Current reconstruction checkpoint 2026-08-01: live graph has 2,266 nodes including three historical missing endpoints, 10,495 deduplicated directed edges, one connected component, zero active isolates, and zero active degree-one nodes. Stored dependencies total 8,872: related 5,403, implements 2,147, discovered_from 291, parent 275, blocked_by 238, blocks 231, verifies 181, supersedes 56, related_to 40, child 8, incident_from 2. The 11 audit findings are informational terminal-only debt: one legacy duplicate class, one retired sentinel class, eight historical ordering-cycle components, and three dangling terminal references. Active enrichment can proceed with evidence-backed typed edges; terminal cleanup remains isolated in pm-hnc9w7, pm-lnrk, and pm-s5e04g so history and changelog truth are preserved."
  "2026-08-01T20:25:23.217Z","harness:codex","Checkpoint result 2026-08-01: typed enrichment added four ordering prerequisites and six verification relationships, plus the versioned recurrence lineage for pm-449do9. Edge count increased from 10,495 to 10,515 while active isolate and degree-one counts stayed zero. The change is semantic rather than density-driven: capture and identity now order provenance reads and analytics; judged corpora order context evaluation; quality, recovery, exit, parity, and SDK exemplars point to the outcomes they prove."
notes[2]:
  - created_at: "2026-07-25T00:00:23.513Z"
    author: maintainer-agent
    text: "Depth baseline measured 2026-07-25, before and after an active-graph enrichment pass. This is the first census that separates semantic edges from hierarchy, which turns out to be the measurement that matters.\n\nMethod. Parse every item file directly for parent and dependency edges, build two undirected graphs — one over all edge kinds, one excluding parent and child — and run breadth-first search from the outcome milestone roots over each. Hierarchy-inclusive reachability flatters the graph badly, so it is reported separately and should not be used as a health signal.\n\nBefore, over 218 active items: 2 items with zero semantic edges, both of them capability epics (the MCP platform epic and the observability epic — the two hubs least likely to be suspected); 57 items with exactly one; 44 items unreachable from any outcome milestone by semantic edges alone; maximum semantic hop distance 3, with hierarchy carrying almost all of the apparent connectivity.\n\nAfter: zero items with no semantic edge; 29 with exactly one, of which 27 are Semgrep findings sitting correctly in their deliberate two-level rule-class hub topology and one is the recorded deliberately-shallow item that must never receive fabricated edges; 0 unreachable; semantic hop distance now distributes across 0 to 6, meaning traversal actually traverses. Workspace edge count moved 3,478 to 3,764, entirely in the related kind and entirely on active items.\n\nThe finding worth keeping. The audit's isolated-node and degree-at-most-one counters both read zero before this pass, while 44 active items could not reach any strategic outcome without walking a parent edge. Those counters measure whether an item is attached, not whether it is explained. Depth, eccentricity, and shortest typed path to an outcome are the properties that make graph algorithms useful for context assembly, and none of them were being measured. That gap is now owned by pm-bzmeaa.\n\nConstraint honoured. No closed or canceled item was touched in this pass. Terminal lineage remains the exclusive territory of the dedicated changelog-safe waves — pm-lnrk for closed lineage, pm-hnc9w7 for legacy edge hygiene, pm-s5e04g for evidence-derived edges — precisely because touching a terminal item moves its timestamp and drags years-old work into the current release notes."
  - created_at: "2026-07-25T06:30:14.336Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Graph measurement and enrichment pass on 2026-07-25, following the earlier measurement recorded in the preceding note. Method is unchanged and remains canonical: parse the .toon corpus directly (dependencies[N]{...} CSV blocks, not the CLI renderer, which is far too slow past two hundred items), build two undirected graphs - all-kinds and semantic-only, meaning every kind except parent and child - and breadth-first search each from the Milestone-type roots. Hierarchy-inclusive reachability always flatters; report semantic-only.\n\nBefore this pass: 3,832 workspace edges, 1,811 semantic edges, 36 active items at semantic degree one, semantic depth 6, zero unreachable, zero zero-degree. After: 3,989 workspace edges, 1,872 semantic edges, 28 active items at semantic degree one, semantic depth 6, zero unreachable, zero zero-degree. The 28 remaining degree-one items are exactly the deliberate Semgrep two-level hub topology (members to file representative to rule-class representative) and must never be given fabricated edges.\n\nThe substantive change this pass was edge-kind diversity rather than edge count. Two registered relationship kinds had never been used in this workspace: implements had zero edges and verifies had eight. They now carry ten and nineteen. The distinction encoded is worth preserving because graph queries depend on it: `implements` points from a delivery item to the story or accepted decision it realises, so traversing incoming implements edges on a story answers what work would satisfy it; `verifies` points from a gate, benchmark, or harness to the property it supplies evidence for, so traversing incoming verifies edges on an outcome milestone answers what would prove the gate is met. Every outcome milestone now has at least one incoming verifies edge, which makes the milestone ladder traversable in the evidence direction and not only in the ownership direction.\n\nThe other structural gain was the consolidation family. Thirteen children of the simplification epic held exactly one semantic edge each - blocked_by the alias shim - which made them indistinguishable from one another to any graph algorithm. Each now carries the defects and owners it actually absorbs (calendar relocation to the duration-parsing defect and the calendar service collision; ops grouping to the three diagnostics-surface defects; annotation facets to the linked-test ordering and stdin conventions, and so on). Those edges are class relationships that already existed in the ledger prose and are now machine-readable.\n\nStanding caution repeated from the first pass: isolate and degree counters measure attachment, not explanation. `pm graph audit` reported zero isolated and zero degree-leq-one active nodes both before and after this pass, while the semantic measurements above moved substantially. Strategic reachability, eccentricity, and shortest typed path to a milestone are the metrics that matter and they are owned by pm-bzmeaa."
    edited_at: "2026-07-25T06:32:42.325Z"
plan_mode: approved
plan_resume_context: "Current checkpoint 2026-08-03: 2,296 items, 43,816 immutable events, 10,761 deduplicated graph edges, one component, zero active isolates, zero active degree-one nodes, ten layers, and only eleven classified informational legacy findings. Every active item has AC, estimate, risk, confidence, and dependencies; the roadmap is the sole intentional parent root. Three unique future features were filed for automatic semantic session attribution, cross-harness provenance adapters, and history-derived CI recurrence. Terminal metadata and links remain evidence-batched under pm-e9zh, pm-j8z6, pm-hnc9w7, and pm-lnrk."
plan_validation[1]{text,command,expected}:
  All-status baseline must remain reproducible and append-only before any terminal enrichment batch.,pm validate --check-history-drift --check-storage-integrity --check-lifecycle --check-resolution --counts --json,"Zero history-chain, storage-integrity, lifecycle, active-blocker, and active-cycle errors; historical metadata debt remains explicitly classified rather than placeholder-normalized."
plan_decisions[1]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-08-03T11:10:30.966Z","harness:codex","Optimize relationship semantics, reachability, and explainability rather than raw edge density.","The graph is already one connected component with no active isolates. Adding weak related edges would inflate degree while degrading planning, impact, and critical-path meaning.","2026-08-03 graph audit: 10,704 deduplicated directed edges, zero active isolates, 67 redundant edges, ten layers, and only informational legacy findings."
plan_discoveries[3]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T11:10:31.658Z","harness:codex","Automatic author harness and instance detection works for current Codex mutations, but model, effort, role, and topic are all explicitly null; corpus-wide topic and role observations remain zero."
  "2026-08-03T11:11:51.782Z","harness:codex","Correction to the preceding provenance discovery: automatic harness and instance detection works for current Codex mutations, whose model, effort, role, and topic are all explicitly null. Across all 43,787 events, model is present on 0, effort on 702, role on 37, and topic on 0; role is sparse, not zero. Immutable history preserves the superseded statement and this correction."
  "2026-08-03T11:29:07.574Z","harness:codex","Fresh hybrid reindex completed, but its checked-in 10-query relevance evaluation failed 6 queries at average nDCG@5 0.7014 while the separately wired 5-query k=10 retrieval CI gate passed at nDCG 0.8327. Canonical owner pm-p1g43q now records the split; future context/retrieval work must converge fixture topology, thresholds, k, and published metrics rather than treating either result as universal."
